  "judge": {
    "verdict": "QUESTIONED",
    "report": "# Judge Report: regression-v1 (Session 337116)\n\n## Executive Summary\n**QUESTIONED.** All 74 knowledge entries report a perfect fitness of 1.0 with zero variance, and the population was apparently at this value from generation 0 onward. The Mann-Whitney U test returned p=NaN due to this zero-variance condition, meaning the improvement test is statistically undefined and uninterpretable. While shallow AST depths, healthy operator entropy, and moderate noise resilience appear superficially positive, the fundamental absence of any evolutionary trajectory \u2014 combined with zero ADF learning \u2014 makes this experiment unable to demonstrate that the cognitive engine contributed meaningfully to the solution. The results are consistent with a fitness function that is too permissive or a problem that is too trivial for this configuration.\n\n## Metric Review\n| Metric | Value | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fitness mean | 1.0 | \u26a0\ufe0f Uniformly perfect \u2014 suspicious for zero variance |\n| Fitness CI | [1.0, 1.0] | \u26a0\ufe0f Confirms zero spread; no discrimination between solutions |\n| Fitness std | 0.0 | \ud83d\udd34 Red flag \u2014 all 74 entries identical |\n| Mann-Whitney p | NaN | \ud83d\udd34 Test is undefined; cannot draw any statistical conclusion |\n| Mann-Whitney effect | 0.0 (negligible) | \ud83d\udd34 Uninterpretable due to NaN p-value |\n| AST depth mean | 1.91 | \u2705 Low complexity; low overfitting risk |\n| AST depth max | 4 | \u2705 Acceptable; no runaway growth |\n| ADF entries | 0 | \u26a0\ufe0f No new functions learned \u2014 limited cognitive contribution |\n| Operator entropy | 0.969 (normalized) | \u2705 Excellent operator diversity |\n| Stagnation | Yes, from generation 0 | \ud83d\udd34 Fitness never changed during evolution |\n| Convergence speed | Gen 0 / ratio 0.0 | \u26a0\ufe0f \"Converged\" instantly \u2014 no evolutionary process observed |\n| Noise resilience (\u03c3=0.2) | 0.924 \u00b1 0.014 | \u2705 Moderate robustness under stress |\n\n## Deep Dive Findings\n\n### 1. Statistical Test Failure (Mann-Whitney U)\nThe p=NaN result is not a minor anomaly \u2014 it means the Mann-Whitney U test could not be computed because one or both groups have zero variance (all values are 1.0). This is a **hard statistical failure**, not a borderline result. The test requires at least some distributional spread to produce a meaningful p-value. Without it, we have **no statistical basis** to claim improvement or non-improvement.\n\n### 2. Perfect Fitness with Zero Variance\nBootstrap CI confirms mean=1.0, std=0.0 across all 74 entries. In any realistic regression domain, achieving perfect fitness universally across the entire knowledge base with zero exceptions is extraordinary and warrants scrutiny. Possible explanations:\n- The problem is trivially solvable (e.g., fitting y = x with minimal noise)\n- The fitness function saturates at 1.0 for any \"reasonable\" answer\n- Precision or tolerance thresholds are set too loosely\n\n### 3. Complete Stagnation from Generation 0\nThe rolling variance is 0.0 across every window, and convergence speed is 0.0 (reached threshold at generation 0). This means **no evolution occurred** \u2014 the population started at maximum fitness and stayed there. There is no learning trajectory to analyze.\n\n### 4. Operator Entropy is Healthy\nShannon entropy of 2.25 (normalized 0.969) indicates the 8 operators across 5 types are used near-uniformly with no dead or dominant operators. This is a positive signal for the genetic diversity of the search, but it is moot if fitness discrimination is absent.\n\n### 5. AST Complexity is Low but Expected\nWith max depth 4 and mean 1.91, programs are very small. The distribution (depth 1: 33, 2: 32, 3: 7, 4: 2) suggests mostly single- or double-operator expressions. For an algebraic regression domain, this is plausible but also consistent with trivially simple target functions. The \"low\" overfitting risk is correct but provides little insight when all solutions are identical in fitness.\n\n### 6. Stress Test Shows Moderate Robustness\nDegradation at \u03c3=0.2 is 7.6%, which is acceptable. However, this tests sensitivity to output noise, not whether the solutions are genuinely correct or merely \"good enough\" under a lenient fitness metric.\n\n## Verdict\n**QUESTIONED**\n\nThe core issue is that this experiment produces no interpretable evidence of cognitive engine performance. A result of uniform fitness=1.0 from generation 0, combined with a failed statistical test (p=NaN), means:\n- We cannot confirm the engine improved anything\n- We cannot confirm the solutions are genuinely optimal vs. merely acceptable\n- We cannot distinguish this run from a random search that happened to land on acceptable programs immediately\n\nThe results are **not falsified** \u2014 they may be legitimate for a trivially easy problem \u2014 but they are **unverifiable** as a demonstration of the Logos V9 engine's capabilities.\n\n## Recommendations\n- **Re-run with a harder regression target** (e.g., multi-term nonlinear functions, noisy data, or symbolic regression benchmarks like Nguyen benchmarks) to generate a non-trivial fitness landscape\n- **Lower the fitness tolerance or use a stricter fitness function** (e.g., raw MSE instead of a capped/scaled metric) to enable discrimination between solutions\n- **Add baseline comparison runs** (random search, hill climbing, or a simpler GP) so the Mann-Whitney test has a meaningful control group\n- **Record and report generation-by-generation fitness distributions** (min, max, median, IQR) \u2014 the current reporting of only aggregate metrics hides the evolutionary trajectory\n- **Investigate why ADFs were never created** \u2014 0 ADF entries suggests the architecture was underutilized; check if ADF creation operators were enabled or if mutation/crossover pressure was insufficient\n- **Manually inspect several of the 74 solutions** to verify they actually solve their target regression tasks \u2014 fitness=1.0 should correspond to a correct symbolic expression, and this should be validated independently of the pipeline",
